preConditionHook:
// The single-bar measured move: project one bar's own high-low height beyond
// that bar's far extreme. PatternHeightMeasuredMoveTarget with the reference
// window collapsed to one bar, which is why it needs no window state.
// The reference bar is read UNCONDITIONALLY: EasyLanguage does not
// short-circuit (EL_LogicalEval_Probe), so the subscript is reached on every
// bar however it is guarded, and Max Bars Back must cover refBar regardless.
// Only the freeze is conditional. BarsSinceEntry() is 0 on the fill bar and 0
// while flat (VERIFIED), so refBar = 1 is the SIGNAL bar under the standing
// signal-bar-close / next-bar-open convention, and the capture re-arms on
// every flat bar. Freezing at entry -- rather than recomputing off the rolling
// offset -- is what holds the target still while the position is open.
// refBar is a double input used as a subscript; the narrowing is deliberate.
// tolerancePoints is in PRICE UNITS: MinMove / PriceScale are UNKNOWN.
barHigh = high[refBar];
barLow = low[refBar];
if (el_eq((double)ctx.BarsSinceEntry(), 0.0)) {
    refHigh = barHigh;
    refLow = barLow;
}
